          %title
          %p There are several notions under a name of compatible localization; where localization pertains to the localization of rings or of localization of categories.
          %h2#pairwise_compatibility_of_a_family_of_localizations (Pairwise) compatibility of a family of localizations
          %p
            Consider a family of localizations sharing the same source ring (or source category). Two Gabriel localizations
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_{R k}: R\to R_k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 1,2
            of a ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi k
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_{k}:M\to M_k
            are mutually compatible if the consecutive localization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mn 1
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_2 Q_1 R
            is naturally a ring and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mn 2
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_1 Q_2 R
            is a ring (semi-compatible if just one of the two), such that the corresponding localization arrow is a morphism of rings. This is equivalent to the following more general criterium.
          %p
            Two
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+localization"} affine localization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Q
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_k^*
            and direct image functors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_{k*}: A\to A_k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 1,2
            are mutually compatible if the endofunctors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi k
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo *
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Q
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_k:=Q_{k*}Q_k^*
            mutually commute as endofunctors of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            According to Thomason-Trobaugh, an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+scheme"} algebraic scheme
            is
            %strong semiseparated
            if it has an affine cover such that the intersection of any two affines in the cover is affine (semiseparated cover). For example, every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated+scheme"} separated scheme
            is semiseparated.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"} Alexander Rosenberg
            extends this terminology to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+scheme"} noncommutative scheme
          %h2#compatible_ore_localizations Compatible Ore localizations
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be two Ore sets in a domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mi T
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_T:R\to T^{-1}R
            the canonical map. Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_T(S)
            is left Ore in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^{-1}R
            if for every
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\in T
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in S
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s'\in S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r'\in R
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t'\in T
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ′
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi r
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %msup
                    %mo ′
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi r
                  %mo ′
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s' t^{-1} r = t'^{-1}r' s
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^{-1} R
            = succeed "(This" do
              %br/
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi r
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mi s
                  %msup
                    %mo ′
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi t
                  %msup
                    %mo ′
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi r
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t^{-1}r s^{-1} = s'^{-1}t'^{-1}r'
            in the module
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^{-1}S^{-1}T^{-1}R
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r = 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{s}\in S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{r}\in R
            so that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{s}r = \tilde{r} r
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_1\in T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_1\in S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_1\in R
            so that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_1 t^{-1} = t^{-1}_1 r_1 \tilde{s}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_1 t^{-1} r = t_1^{-1} r_1\tilde{s} r = t_1^{-1}(r_1\tilde{r})s
          %p
            This could be found more readily by computing in the ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T\vee S)^{-1} R
            or module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^{-1}S^{-1}T^{-1}R
            where the above condition is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi r
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mi s
                  %msup
                    %mo ′
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi t
                  %msup
                    %mo ′
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi r
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t^{-1}r s^{-1} = s'^{-1}t'^{-1}r'
            \. This can be interpreted also as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{-1} T^{-1} R\subset T^{-1}S^{-1}R
            within
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi S
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T\vee S)^{-1} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r = 1
            case by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi r
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi s
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msubsup
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t^{-1} r s^{-1} = t^{-1}\tilde{s}^{-1}\tilde{r} = s_1^{-1}t_1^{-1}r_1\tilde{r}
          %h2#coaction_compatible_localizations Coaction compatible localizations
          %p
            Given a right
            = succeed "-comodule" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E, \rho)
            for a bialgebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho : E\to E\otimes H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : E\to E'
            is
            = succeed "-compatible" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho': E'\to E\otimes H
            such that the following diagram commutes:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi j
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                          %mo ′
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mi ρ
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo ′
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi H
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi j
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi H
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  E &amp; \stackrel{j}\to &amp; E'\\
                  \\downarrow\rho &amp;&amp; \downarrow \rho'\\
                  E\otimes H &amp;\stackrel{j\otimes H}\to &amp; E'\otimes H
                  }
          %h2#compatibility_of_localizations_and_endofunctors Compatibility of localizations and endofunctors
          %p
            A localization functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Q
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q^*=Q^*_\Sigma : A\to B
            (not necessarily having a right adjoint) universally inverting a family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            of morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is compatible with an endofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G:A\to A
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(\Sigma)\subset \Sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi Σ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\Sigma\in B
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Q
                      %mo *
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi Σ
                    %msup
                      %mi Q
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q^* G = G_\Sigma Q^*
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q^*
            is a localization having a fully faithful right adjoint
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            (which is hence iso) and unit
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q^*
            with an endofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is equivalent to any of the following:
          %p
            (i) there exists a distributive law
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi l
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l : Q_* Q^* G\to G Q_* Q^*
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_* Q^*
            is understood as (the underlying functor of) the idempotent monad induced by the adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q^*\dashv Q_*
          %p
            (ii) the natural transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                  %mi G
                  %mi η
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q^* G\eta : Q^* G\to Q^* G Q_* Q^*
            is invertible
          %p
            (iii) there is a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G'
            and a natural isomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Q
                      %mo *
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi G
                    %mo ′
                    %msup
                      %mi Q
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q^* G\cong G' Q^*
          %p
            If (i) holds then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l
            is invertible and uniquely determined by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and the monad
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Q
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q^* Q_*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi Σ
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_* G_\Sigma \neq G Q_*
            in general. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/zoranskoda/show/distributive+law+for+idempotent+monad"} distributive law for idempotent monad
            for more.
          %p
            One can also consider the distributive laws
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
